  "historical_output_text": " **How to Plant a Tomato Seedling**\n\nGrowing your own tomatoes from a seedling can be incredibly rewarding. Here’s how to do it:\n\n1. **Choose the Right Spot:**\n   Find a sunny spot in your garden or a sunny windowsill if you’re planting indoors. Tomatoes need at least 6-8 hours of direct sunlight a day. This is crucial for the plant to produce fruit and stay healthy.\n\n2. **Prepare Your Pot or Garden Bed:**\n   Ensure the soil is well-draining and rich in organic matter. For a pot, use a container with good drainage holes. For a garden bed, remove any weeds and loosen the soil to a depth of about 12 inches. This step is essential for the roots to grow properly and access nutrients.\n\n3. **Plant the Seedling:**\n   Gently remove the tomato plant from its container without damaging the roots. If it’s in a peat pot, you can plant the whole pot; just make sure the top of the soil is level with the surface. If the plant has multiple leaves, you can bury the stem up to the first set of leaves. This helps",
